Z||000005||stimpy||04-07-2000||07:50 PM||||I would like to find out if any interior kits for these cars are available. I had the opportunity to take a closeup look at one and they do have very nice innards... rosewood panels, glovebox, leather doorpanels, sheepskin carpeting, grommeted leather seats (kinda Lambo-looking). Pretty slick.  <BR>But thats a whole LOTTA chrome!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||04-07-2000||08:06 PM||||They didn't make many of the Zimmers and they were $54K when new. There wereless than 100 made (I think only 67).  Bob Steiger has one in his storage bay in Illinois.  I found a wrecked one for a parts car at Kick Hill Farms. They were professional rebodies made in Florida all hand tooled inside, wood inlay, all leather interiors.  I've only seen 3 at any of the Fiero shows I attended in the last five years.  They are a kind of car you either love or hate. For you people going to TWIN LAKES Fiero on 5/6, Bob may have it out.  He was getting some rechroming done the last I knew. He may take it to the Dells this year.<P>The one for $29K is only for collectors.  Top speed was maybe 105, and the handeling was questionable with the long front end.||||reg||10
